- The errors are jointly normal, and $\theta_W, \theta_H$ are estimated as free parameters.

$$
\begin{aligned}
t_H&=\beta_H z^{T,H}+\frac{\gamma_H}{\sqrt{\theta_H w_H}}+\gamma_{WH}\sqrt{\frac{\theta_W w_W}{\theta_H w_H}}+v_H,\\[.4em]
t_W&=\beta_W z^{T,W}+\frac{\gamma_W}{\sqrt{\theta_W w_W}}+\gamma_{WH}\sqrt{\frac{\theta_H w_H}{\theta_W w_W}}+v_W,\\[.4em]
m^*&=\alpha z^T+\gamma_W\sqrt{\theta_W w_W}+\gamma_H\sqrt{\theta_H w_H}+u,\\
m&=\begin{cases}m^*,&m^*\ge0,\\0,&m^*<0.\end{cases}
\end{aligned}
$$

The estimated system is equations (9)–(12), manuscript PDF page 29; the two time equations are uncensored and purchased care is Tobit-censored. The theoretical corner switches shadow prices by a common multiplier, but this regime switch is omitted from the time equations in estimation (PDF page 32). [View equations and estimation discussion](/research/household-demand-leisure/sources/#pdf-page-29).
